  "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $B$ to the line $\\overset{\u27f7}{AC},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{\u27f7}{AC}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/5ebb72b8b79beefebac6ebd4a34cf229bc644d48a8de711eda1f2e20c31a67ec.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $B$ to $\\overset{\u27f7}{AC}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/df918f525274479ddf12fd1940408be116c92dbe93ca19e46676ec07dc5121a8.png)",
